WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.930
Satoshi and Go went to Galar
in order to watch the Pokémon World Championships.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.490
Kyodaimax!

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:33.990
Before the excitement had a chance to die down,
Team Rocket attempted to catch a Pokémon...

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.180
...which ended up Kyodaimaxing!

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.060
<i>Nyah, nyah!</i>

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.320
Come over here, why don'tcha?!

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.870
Oh, what is this?!

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.370
A Kyodaimax Kajirigame
is going on a rampage!

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.490
Come on!

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.140
Yeah!

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.140
This way, Pikachu!

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:03.120
You too, Hibunny!

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:11.920
PocketMonsters

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.340
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.920
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.640
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.510
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.850
Be it through fire or through water

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.520
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.020
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:37.280
Each and every one of my memories

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.870
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.790
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:51.540
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.550
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:02.760
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.100
Let's have a fight!

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.810
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.640
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.980
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:19.650
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:24.990
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.490
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:31.620
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.420
I choose you!

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.430
The Path to Power!!
Satoshi VS Dande!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.570
Hey! Calm down!

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:58.450
If you don't stop,
you might wreck the entire stadium!

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.240
Looks like we'll just
have to battle it!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.220
Huh?!

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.720
We'll draw its attention with a battle
and get it away from the stadium!

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:13.480
But how are you planning
to fight a Daimax Pokémon?

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.220
I dunno!

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.090
“I dunno”?!

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.710
All the more reason to try!

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.500
You stand back, Go!

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.080
I refuse!

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.600
If you're fighting, then so am I!

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.600
All right! Time for a tag battle!

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.810
Yeah!

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.600
Pikachu, let's do this!

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.510
Us, too, Hibunny!

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.350
100,000 Volts!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.120
Use Double Kick!

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.080
No good!

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.010
Here it comes!

00:03:59.010 --> 00:03:59.920
Yeah!

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.090
Electroweb!

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.360
What's up, Pikachu?

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.080
Hey, Satoshi, isn't that...?

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.610
What?!

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:45.190
Pikachu Daimaxed?!

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.350
Satoshi!

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.530
Pikachu!
Just use Lightning Speed!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.660
Satoshi!
The stadium's still full of people!

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.550
I know!

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.020
Pikachu, use Iron Tail!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.070
A Kyodaimax Pikachu?

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.420
Great job, Pikachu!

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:02.960
No way...

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:09.930
That young man's battling
<i>without</i> a Daimax Band?

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.170
That's...

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:20.290
The Rock-type Daimax move!

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.060
Tell him to use
Kyodai Heavy Thunder!

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.110
Mr. Dande?!

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.870
Your Pikachu should be able to use it!
Kyodai Heavy Thunder!

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.870
Right! I'll give it a try!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.210
Pikachu!
Kyodai Heavy Thunder!

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.660
Did we do it?

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.330
I see! Kyodai Heavy Thunder, huh?

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.470
That was amazing, Pikachu!

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.170
Now's our chance!

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:36.120
Let's get that Daimax Pokémon!

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.310
Hurry, meow!

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:43.670
You two!

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:45.030
Are you all right?

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.570
Yeah, we're fine!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:50.320
Mr. Dande,
thanks for the help!

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:52.820
I'm the one who should
be thanking you.

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:55.490
I'm Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.330
I'm Go from Kuchiba City!

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.040
I'm Dande.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.080
We know!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.000
You're the World Champion, yeah?

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.210
I'd like to ask you something.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.500
Wait… Ask him?

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.860
Please battle me!

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.320
Satoshi! How crazy can you get?!

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:19.590
Hey! You can't Kyodaimax
your Pokémon here!

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:20.970
No, you got it all wrong!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.380
We were acting as bait
to lure that big one away!

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:28.400
They are the heroes
who saved the stadium!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.420
Show them some respect.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.660
Oh, pardon me!

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:38.440
PocketMonsters

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.130
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:44.500
PocketMonsters

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:49.420
Rock
Water
Kajirigame
PocketMonsters

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.280
The Galar Region's scones
really are great, huh, Satoshi?

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.280
Satoshi?

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.290
Hey...

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.150
You're so out of it that
you won't even <i>eat</i>?

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.340
A Pokémon I've
never seen before!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.930
Hoshigarisu! Cheek-Stuffing Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:25.010
It eats berries nonstop!

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:30.310
When its cheeks are full,
it tends to stash more in the flaps in its tail!

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.380
Monster Ball, go!

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:45.850
Hoshigarisu's data will be
added to the Index!

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.950
All right!
That's my second Galar Pokémon!

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:56.970
Satoshi, something troubling you?
Then you should tell me!

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.940
Oh, I was just remembering
Mr. Dande's battle yesterday!

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.970
Oh, I see...

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:05.580
Huh? Can't I?

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:10.960
You think about Pokémon
or battling 24/7, huh?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:15.620
No, I totally space out
if I don't get ten hours of sleep.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:18.510
So that's 24 hours minus 10,
which is...

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.710
Never mind that.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:24.090
The point is, you want to
battle Mr. Dande, right?

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.980
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.400
All right, I get it.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:32.400
But getting to battle him
will be tough.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.410
Huh?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:38.530
If you want to participate in
the Pokémon World Championships,

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:43.040
you'll have to sign up online,
and then win your way up through the ranks.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.790
Ranks?

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.790
Your position, based on
your record and performance.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:51.960
The top 8 in the rankings
are called the Master Class.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:56.810
At the end of the season,
those eight fight in a tournament,

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:59.680
where the winner
becomes the Champion.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.680
So I can battle Mr. Dande
if I enter that?!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.040
Think it'll be that easy?!

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:06.680
Why not?

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:14.140
Trainers who enter get divided into four classes based off
their win/lose ratio and the contents of their battles.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:18.070
All trainers entering for the first time
go into the Normal Class.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:21.570
Then the trainers in that rank
battle it out between each other,

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.840
and the ones ranked 999 to 100
enter the Super Class.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:30.370
Above that, 99 through 9
make up the Hyper Class.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.540
What about Mr. Dande?!

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.880
He's in the highest Master Class,
of course.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.090
And he's ranked number one, at that!

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:41.930
So if you want to battle him,
you'll have to climb your way up to the Master Class!

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.600
Was that too complicated for you?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.470
Well, I just gotta win battles, right?

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.190
Right! Let's do this!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:55.790
Here.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:00.970
You really saved me!

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.510
What?! M-M-Mr. Dande?!

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:05.500
W-W-What are you doing here?!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.770
You said you wanted
to battle me, right?

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:12.670
Um, but I <i>just</i> finished explaining
how that wouldn't be so easy...

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:18.050
As the World Champion,
I thought I'd grant this young man's dream.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.610
Please do!

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.050
What?!

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:29.040
We've been running
all over the place since yesterday...

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.340
...without catching a single thing...

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:35.250
Where'd that Daimax
Pokémon go, meow?

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.820
Hey, Musashi! What's that?!

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.410
What?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:43.820
Who's that Pokémon?!

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:47.330
Kamukame. Snapping Pokémon.
Water type.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:49.910
Evolves into Kajirigame.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.080
Well, ain't that a shocker?

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:57.590
Oh, my! This thing can evolve into
that giant from yesterday, meow!

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.230
That's great!
Get it for me, Kojiro.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.340
A-Are you sure?

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.800
It'll turn into
that ferocious thing, right?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.310
Huh? It doesn't hurt.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.110
This is perfect, meow!

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:15.470
We'll take it back and
offer it up to Sakaki, meow!

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:16.440
All right!

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.690
<i>Mission complete!
What a great feeling!</i>

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:29.790
Mr. Dande requested
that I be the referee!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.360
Counting on you!

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:33.410
Have this, young Satoshi.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.570
It's a Daimax Band.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:43.450
You battled without
a Band yesterday,

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:46.730
but normally,
we use it to control Daimax.

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:47.740
This?

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:48.300
Yeah.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:52.260
And when your Pokémon goes Daimax,
their move names change as well.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.120
I'll handle the rest!

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.690
Normal-type moves
become Dai Attack.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.290
Steel-type moves
become Dai Steel.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:02.320
And Electric-type moves
become Dai Thunder!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.940
Dai Attack, Dai Steel
and Dai Thunder!

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:09.010
Although, your Pikachu
uses Kyodaimax.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.340
Kyodaimax?

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:15.080
In that case, his Electric-type moves
become Kyodai Heavy Thunder.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.940
Kyodai Heavy Thunder...

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:18.460
The move from yesterday, right?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:23.190
In order to use Daimax,
you have to return your Pokémon to its Monster Ball,

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:26.970
and then fill the Ball with the power emerging
from the Band before throwing it.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:30.550
Pikachu won't go inside
his Monster Ball...

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.400
But I'm sure we'll manage!

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.100
All right, Mr. Dande,
I'll be borrowing this!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.510
So cool!

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.870
Now, both sides
send forth your Pokémon!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:55.250
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:57.580
You're the one I choose!
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:07.470
All right! Pikachu and I
both wanted to battle Lizardon!

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:11.590
It seems you understand
your partner Pokémon's feelings!

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:12.680
I'm glad!

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:17.190
Pikachu has the
type advantage here!

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:22.230
But Champion Dande and Lizardon
will never lose any battle!

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.580
Fine by me!

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.860
Let the match begin!

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.870
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.370
Lizardon!
Counter with Thunder Punch!

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:47.630
I knew they'd be strong!

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.220
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.640
Another Thunder Punch!

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.980
Keep going!

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:04.900
Electroweb!

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.760
Don't worry about it!
Keep going!

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:12.940
Air Slash!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.600
Pikachu!

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.920
All right!
Use 100,000 Volts!

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:27.610
Flamethrower!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:45.440
Even Pikachu's signature 100,000 Volts
can't beat that Flamethrower?!

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.040
Don't give up!

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:17.640
Lizardon?!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.860
The Kyodaimax was a success!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.980
Interesting...
This was well worth it!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.530
Return, Lizardon!

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:39.220
Let me show you
a true champion time!

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.160
Kyodaimax!

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.670
Let's do this, Pikachu!

00:17:58.670 --> 00:17:59.510
Dai Attack!

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.410
Use Dai Jet!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:19.280
Hang in there, Pikachu!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.210
Pikachu! Dai Steel!

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:38.010
Lizardon! Dai Thunder!

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:53.400
In that case...

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.650
Kyodai Heavy Thunder!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.760
Now, enjoy the climax!

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:06.500
Kyodai Hellfire!

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:17.760
They're evenly matched...

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.250
It's not over yet!

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:42.700
Pikachu!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.200
Pikachu is unable to battle!

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:49.070
As such, the winner is
Contestant Dande!

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.590
Looks like it's over...
What a shame, huh, Lizardon?

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:00.590
Pikachu, you gave it your all.

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:06.060
Young Satoshi,
give Pikachu this.

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:07.730
Thank you.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:13.230
Mr. Dande, I'm glad I got to have
a serious battle with you!

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.330
Battles are no fun if
they aren't serious.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.740
That's all there is to it.

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:19.610
Oh, and have this...

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.330
Keep it.

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:21.990
Are you sure?

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:26.740
I like young,
unrefined trainers like you.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:33.240
But if you want to satisfy me,
you'll have to <i>pop</i> more!

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:34.750
“Pop”?

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:38.100
Put on more of a show!

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:39.430
Later, then.

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:44.970
Mr. Dande!
Please, battle me again someday!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.720
Our next match will be
an official one, with a crowd!

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:50.050
Yeah!

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.440
I've made up my mind!

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:58.980
I'll enter the tournament
and battle Mr. Dande again!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.070
And next time, I'll win!

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:03.950
That's the first step towards
becoming a Pokémon Master!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:07.630
That's great!
There's the Satoshi I know!

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.450
Pikachu,
let's get stronger together!

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:31.450
Satoshi, who aims to
battle the World Champion Dande...

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:35.000
And Go, who aims to
catch every Pokémon.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:39.320
Next time, more dreams and adventures
await in the world of Pocket Monsters!

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:41.070
Let's go!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:45.900
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.270
Let's play Pokémon Shiritori!
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:48.410
(Pikachu →<b> Mew Ver.)
Let's play Pokémon Shiritori!
Pokémon Shiritori</b>

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.980
Pokémon Shiritori
(Pikachu →<b> Mew Ver.)</b>

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:49.990
